1
00:00:00,113 --> 00:00:01,163
How many yes or no

2
00:00:01,163 --> 00:00:02,737
questions does it take,

3
00:00:02,737 --> 00:00:03,737
on average,

4
00:00:03,737 --> 00:00:05,025
to guess a hidden letter?

5
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:07,471
In his 1948 paper,

6
00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:08,770
A Mathematical Theory

7
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:09,983
of Communication,

8
00:00:09,983 --> 00:00:12,258
Claude Shannon uses this source:

9
00:00:12,258 --> 00:00:14,695
A half the time, B a quarter,

10
00:00:14,695 --> 00:00:16,820
C and D an eighth each.

11
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:18,095
Ask about the

12
00:00:18,095 --> 00:00:20,021
likeliest letter first.

13
00:00:20,021 --> 00:00:20,933
Is it A?

14
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:21,908
Half the time,

15
00:00:21,908 --> 00:00:23,308
one question is enough.

16
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,450
If not: is it B?

17
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:26,675
Then: is it C?

18
00:00:26,675 --> 00:00:28,350
B takes two questions;

19
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:30,100
C and D take three.

20
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,650
Weight each count by its chance:

21
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:33,950
a half times one,

22
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,100
a quarter times two,

23
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,837
an eighth times three, twice.

24
00:00:37,837 --> 00:00:39,275
One point seven five.

25
00:00:39,887 --> 00:00:41,588
A letter with chance one over two

26
00:00:41,588 --> 00:00:43,800
to the k takes k questions:

27
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,975
log base two of one over p,

28
00:00:45,975 --> 00:00:46,950
its surprise.

29
00:00:47,554 --> 00:00:48,567
The average surprise

30
00:00:48,567 --> 00:00:51,217
is Shannon's entropy, H.

31
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:53,205
Here, one point seven five bits.

32
00:00:53,787 --> 00:00:56,800
Write yes as zero and no as one,

33
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,162
and the questions become a code:

34
00:00:58,575 --> 00:01:01,625
zero, one zero, one one zero,

35
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:02,500
one one one.

36
00:01:03,163 --> 00:01:05,375
Four A's, two B's,

37
00:01:05,375 --> 00:01:08,200
a C and a D take fourteen bits.

38
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:09,425
Two questions per letter

39
00:01:09,425 --> 00:01:10,650
would take sixteen.

40
00:01:11,271 --> 00:01:13,396
Fourteen bits over eight letters is

41
00:01:13,396 --> 00:01:15,745
one point seven five per letter:

42
00:01:15,745 --> 00:01:17,596
the entropy, the average number of

43
00:01:17,596 --> 00:01:19,295
yes or no questions.
